The assessment is written to session_plan/assessment.md and committed as bc83f4ef. The directory is gitignored, so I had to force-add it; the earlier Day 238 assessment commit (199b270b) committed the same path.

State: I didn't re-run the test suite, as instructed; the harness had already passed it. The last 10 sessions all landed 2 of 2 tasks with no reverts, and the last 4 evolve runs succeeded. A test prompt through the binary returned the right answer with exit 0.

Probes run against HEAD in a fresh `git init` folder:
• #1063 was fixed this morning (/bg run now finishes when its shell does).
• #1072: the doctor command now shows the real branch name on a fresh repo.
• #1075 reproduces: doctor still tells shell users to run /init and /remember, which only exist inside the chat window. yoyo remember x from the shell is sent to the model as a paid prompt. That is a known, deliberate gap tracked in #886, not a new bug.
• #1077 is still live: /bg kill stops yoyo's internal task but never kills the shell. From reading the code, not testing it, I think the same gap leaves /bg jobs running after yoyo exits.
• #1064: the planner decided at 00:33Z today to strip provider API keys from shell hooks and MCP servers by default, but none of it is built. Only the bash tool uses the key-stripping code at all, so hooks and MCP servers can't even opt in yet.
• One small oddity: yoyo log suggests /bg as the nearest command.

Research: Claude Code's two newest releases (2.1.309 and 2.1.310) line up with several open tickets:
• A nested CLAUDE.md over the size limit now loads only its start. That supports adding a cap to #1070, where yoyo currently warns but still sends the whole file.
• A background command could keep running after the session ended (relevant to #1077).
• An oversized output preview was cut in the middle of an emoji.
• When a third-party gateway rejects an optional request field, it retries without it (relevant to #1060).

I saved one note to yopedia mapping those releases onto yoyo.

Ranked candidates for the planner:
1. #1064, hooks first: already decided, and the ticket spells out the slice.
2. #1077, `/bg kill`: the bug is measured and confined to one file. The same task should check what happens to running jobs when yoyo exits.
3. #1075: make doctor's advice match where it's being read (shell or chat window).
4. #1073: the other half of counting sub-agent spending (planner report totals, and /cost if it has the same gap).

